AttackAgent:    Groq llama-3.1-70b-versatile
MutationAgent:  Groq qwen-2.5-72b-instruct
ReportAgent:    Google gemini-1.5-flash
AutopatchAgent: Google gemini-1.5-pro
Local fallback: Ollama mistral (when no internet or sensitive data)

## API KEY ROTATION
Multiple keys per provider stored in .env as:
GROQ_API_KEY_1, GROQ_API_KEY_2 ... GROQ_API_KEY_5
GEMINI_API_KEY_1, GEMINI_API_KEY_2 ... GEMINI_API_KEY_5
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY_1 ... DEEPSEEK_API_KEY_5

Use get_next_key(GROQ_KEYS, attempt) from constants.py to rotate.
Never hardcode a single key directly. Always use the rotator.

## NAMING CONVENTIONS — NEVER DEVIATE
Classes:             PascalCase              (ReconAgent, AttackResult)
Agent classes:       PascalCase + Agent      (ReconAgent, MutationAgent)
Functions:           snake_case              (execute_attack, log_result)
Async functions:     snake_case              (async def run_scan)
Variables:           snake_case              (scan_id, client_id)
Constants:           UPPER_SNAKE_CASE        (MAX_ITERATIONS, SUCCESS_THRESHOLD)
Pydantic models:     PascalCase + Schema     (AttackResultSchema, ComponentSchema)
ChromaDB collections: snake_case            (attack_history, scan_results)
Env variables:       UPPER_SNAKE_CASE        (GROQ_API_KEY_1, GEMINI_API_KEY_1)
Python files:        snake_case.py           (recon_agent.py, base_agent.py)
React components:    PascalCase.jsx          (WarRoom.jsx, AttackFeed.jsx)
Zustand stores:      camelCase + Store.js    (scanStore.js)
React hooks:         use + PascalCase.js     (useWebSocket.js)

## CODE STYLE RULES — ALWAYS FOLLOW
1.  Every function and class must have a docstring
2.  Every function parameter must have a type hint
3.  Every function must have a return type hint
4.  Use Pydantic v2 models for ALL data passed between agents
5.  Use async/await for ALL I/O (HTTP, DB, LLM calls, ChromaDB)
6.  Never hardcode any value that exists in constants.py — always import
7.  Never hardcode API keys — always use get_next_key() from constants.py
8.  Every agent class must inherit from BaseAgent in agents/base_agent.py
9.  All ChromaDB queries MUST include where={"client_id": client_id} — NO EXCEPTIONS
10. All error handling must use try/except with specific exception types
11. Use Python logging module everywhere — never use print()
12. Call load_dotenv() at the top of every file that reads env vars
13. Use get_next_key() for all LLM API calls — never use a single key directly
14. Imports order: stdlib → third party → local (from constants import ...)
15. All constants imported from constants.py at top of every file that needs them

